msgid "Update"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"It is with great pleasure that we are announcing the release of Quarkus 3.8,\n"
"our new LTS release (see https://quarkus.io/blog/lts-releases/[this blog "
"post] for more information about our LTS releases)."
msgstr ""

msgid "LTS releases are maintained for a period of 12 months."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The previous LTS release was 3.2 and a lot of exciting new features have "
"been added to Quarkus since then."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"As we explained in https://quarkus.io/blog/our-plans-for-quarkus-3-7-3-8-3-9-"
"released/[this blog post], 3.8 is the direct continuation of the 3.7 branch,\n"
"so it doesn't contain any new features compared to 3.7 (at least for core "
"features, see below for new features in Quarkus CXF)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"It contains several additional fixes though, including a CVE fix for https://"
"nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-1597[CVE-2024-1597 - PostgreSQL JDBC "
"Driver]\n"
"(we skipped 3.8.0 to include this particular fix)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"It is a recommended upgrade for everyone, including people using the "
"previous 3.2 LTS."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To update to Quarkus 3.8, we recommend updating to the latest version of the "
"Quarkus CLI and run:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Note that `quarkus update` can update your applications from any version of "
"Quarkus (including 2.x) to Quarkus 3.8."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To migrate from 3.7, you don't have anything to do except updating the "
"version."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you are not already using 3.x, please refer to the https://quarkus.io/"
"blog/quarkus-3-0-final-released/[3.0 announcement] for all the details.\n"
"You can also refer to https://quarkus.io/blog/quarkus-3-upgrade/[this blog "
"post] for additional details.\n"
"Once you upgraded to 3.0, also have a look at the https://github.com/"
"quarkusio/quarkus/wiki/Migration-Guide-3.1[3.1], https://github.com/"
"quarkusio/quarkus/wiki/Migration-Guide-3.2[3.2], https://github.com/"
"quarkusio/quarkus/wiki/Migration-Guide-3.3[3.3], https://github.com/"
"quarkusio/quarkus/wiki/Migration-Guide-3.4[3.4], https://github.com/"
"quarkusio/quarkus/wiki/Migration-Guide-3.5[3.5], and https://github.com/"
"quarkusio/quarkus/wiki/Migration-Guide-3.6[3.6], and https://github.com/"
"quarkusio/quarkus/wiki/Migration-Guide-3.7[3.7] migration guides."
msgstr ""

msgid "What&#8217;s new?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Coming from 3.7?"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Nothing much if you are coming from 3.7 as 3.8 is the direct continuation of "
"3.7."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"It is a recommended upgrade though as 3.8 comes with bugfixes and security "
"fixes."
msgstr ""

msgid "Coming from 3.2 LTS?"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you are coming from our previous LTS, there is a lot to read and you "
"should have a look at our announcements for:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://quarkus.io/blog/quarkus-3-3-0-released/[3.3] - OpenTelemetry "
"improvements, Reactive Messaging Pulsar extension..."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://quarkus.io/blog/quarkus-3-4-1-released/[3.4] - Redis 7.2 and Flyway "
"changes..."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://quarkus.io/blog/quarkus-3-5-0-released/[3.5] - Support for Java 21, "
"OIDC enhancements..."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://quarkus.io/blog/quarkus-3-6-0-released/[3.6] - SSE improvements, "
"OIDC and security-related enhancements..."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://quarkus.io/blog/quarkus-3-7-released/[3.7] - Java 17 as the "
"baseline, Hibernate ORM 6.4, support for Micrometer `@MeterTag`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Make sure you have a look at the migration guides mentioned above when you "
"update from 3.2 to 3.8."
msgstr ""

msgid "Quarkus CXF"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus CXF is part of the Quarkus Platform and has been updated for Quarkus "
"3.8."
msgstr ""

msgid "This new version of Quarkus CXF includes the following changes:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Keeping major.minor version in sync with Quarkus"
msgstr ""

msgid "Logging extension removed from the documentation and code.quarkus.io"
msgstr ""

msgid "Santuario XMLSec extension moved to Quarkus CXF"
msgstr ""

msgid "Improved documentation"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The detailed release notes can be found in the https://docs.quarkiverse.io/"
"quarkus-cxf/dev/release-notes/3.8.0.html[Quarkus CXF documentation]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Full changelog"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can get the full changelog of https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/"
"releases/tag/3.8.1[3.8.1] on GitHub."
msgstr ""

msgid "Contributors"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The Quarkus community is growing and has now https://github.com/quarkusio/"
"quarkus/graphs/contributors[912 contributors].\n"
"Many many thanks to each and everyone of them."
msgstr ""

